/*
Problem: Find Bottom Left Tree Value (LC 513)
Topic: Binary Tree / BFS

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Perform a level order traversal.

The first node processed at every
level is the leftmost node of that
level.

Keep updating the answer with this
node.

After the last level is processed,
the stored node is the bottom-left
value.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Push the root into the queue.

2. While the queue is not empty:

   • Process one complete level.

   • Save the first node of that
     level.

   • Push its left child first,
     then right child.

3. Return the value of the last
   recorded leftmost node.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

          2
        /   \
       1     3

Level 1:

2

Leftmost = 2

Level 2:

1 3

Leftmost = 1

Answer:

1

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

            1
          /   \
         2     3
        /     / \
       4     5   6
            /
           7

Levels:

1

2 3

4 5 6

7

Bottom-left value = 7

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

BFS processes the tree one level at
a time.

Since children are pushed in the
order:

Left → Right

the first node processed at each
level is always that level's
leftmost node.

The final recorded leftmost node is
the answer.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Every node is visited once.

Space : O(n)

Queue may store an entire level.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Binary Tree BFS (Level Order Traversal)
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int findBottomLeftValue(TreeNode* root) {

        if (root == NULL)
            return 0;

        queue<TreeNode*> q;
        q.push(root);

        TreeNode* ans = root;

        while (!q.empty()) {

            int size = q.size();

            // Process one complete level
            for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {

                TreeNode* curr = q.front();
                q.pop();

                // First node of current level
                if (i == 0)
                    ans = curr;

                if (curr->left)
                    q.push(curr->left);

                if (curr->right)
                    q.push(curr->right);
            }
        }

        return ans->val;
    }
};
